  "id": "COMPOUND:35963 - PROTEIN:5011",
  "verbalization": "Picrasin F is implicated in the regulation of HCC1937 through a series of molecular interactions involving a sialyltransferase enzyme. The evidence suggests that Picrasin F acts as a target for multiple compounds, including (1R,8S,9R,16R)-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-9-[(1R,8S,9R,16R)-4,6,12-trihydroxy-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaen-9-yl]-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaene-4,6,12-triol and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. These compounds are all targets of HCC1937, indicating a potential pathway where Picrasin F may influence the activity of these molecules, which in turn affect HCC1937. The integration of these pathways suggests that Picrasin F may act as a modulator of HCC1937 through the regulation of sialyltransferase activity, potentially altering the cellular processes that underlie HCC1937's function. The evidence supports a mechanism where Picrasin F's interaction with sialyltransferase enzymes could lead to changes in HCC1937's activity, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
